  "published": "2026-09-05T11:13:22.39Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "The event layer of the Shared Signals stack, usable on its own. A typed model of a Security Event Token with a builder and a composable validation profile over Abblix JWT, so a token is refused for a missing identifier, a wrong audience or a replay before any handler sees it. Every registered Subject Identifier format has a typed model with polymorphic JSON handling. Delivery models cover push, where the transmitter posts each token, and poll, where the receiver collects and acknowledges them; keys are resolved from the counterparty's JWKS. OpenID Back-Channel Logout rides on the same core, so a relying party validates logout tokens with the same code that validates any other security event. Full details: https://github.com/Abblix/Oidc.Server/releases/tag/v2.4",
